    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d430">

                <pb facs="0497" n="479" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg479"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.3227/9–746: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pawley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-09-07T11:00:00-03:00">September 7, 1946—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 7—10:33 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1570. For Norton and CAB from Landis. Agreement
                        signed.<anchor n="88" xml:id="d430-f1"/> No coastal route and Asuncion is
                    out. Bermuda type. Brazilians full accord with principles and will stick with
                    them, in pending negotiations Argentina, England and Portugal. [Landis.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pawley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
